03:01.830 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:01.860 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:01.890 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:01.920 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:01.950 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:01.980 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.010 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.040 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.070 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.100 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.130 --> 03:03.490
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

03:02.360 --> 03:04.680
I'm so bored.

03:04.680 --> 03:06.160
Yeah...

03:06.460 --> 03:09.080
Think they're busy over there?

03:09.080 --> 03:10.540
I dunno.

03:11.090 --> 03:15.640
But you know, I'm lucky 
you know how to make coffee.

03:16.130 --> 03:17.620
Huh? Why?

03:17.620 --> 03:22.090
Well, one of us has to stay here at the café.

03:22.580 --> 03:26.060
Now I don't have to work with that 
nagging boss of ours,

03:26.060 --> 03:28.260
even if it's just for the summer.

03:30.060 --> 03:31.380
Hey, Ouka...

03:32.630 --> 03:35.770
If you're bored, 
want to practice making coffee?

03:36.110 --> 03:38.170
Huh? Why?

03:39.000 --> 03:41.530
Wow, that's pretty cool!

03:42.470 --> 03:43.690
Excuse me!

03:43.690 --> 03:44.700
Coming!

03:44.700 --> 03:45.660
See ya later.

03:46.120 --> 03:47.630
Thank you for waiting!

03:47.630 --> 03:49.500
We'll get three watermelon parfaits, too.

03:49.500 --> 03:51.000
You got it.

03:51.000 --> 03:53.710
The waitresses here sure are top-class, huh?

03:53.710 --> 03:56.440
Thanks! Come see us every day if you want!

03:57.470 --> 04:01.020
Hey, guys! You came to see us again?

03:59.970 --> 04:02.300
Is that what they call natural talent?

04:02.300 --> 04:05.470
That sociable, friendly vibe she gives off...

04:05.470 --> 04:07.510
She's like that at college, too.

04:07.800 --> 04:11.180
I don't think there's anyone 
who doesn't like Riho-chan.

04:11.180 --> 04:12.560
Huh...

04:12.560 --> 04:14.690
Did she study that somewhere or something?

04:15.210 --> 04:17.000
Interpersonal skills or whatever?

04:17.000 --> 04:18.570
I have no idea.

04:19.130 --> 04:22.950
Riho-chan doesn't usually 
talk about herself that much.

04:22.950 --> 04:24.280
Huh...

04:25.320 --> 04:28.640
Speaking of college, 
you're both in your third year, right?

04:28.640 --> 04:29.450
Yeah.

04:29.450 --> 04:31.020
Not that I'm one to talk,

04:31.020 --> 04:32.920
but shouldn't you be 
looking for permanent jobs?

04:32.920 --> 04:35.390
Uh... I guess so...

04:35.390 --> 04:38.960
I'm all right, though. I have a prospect.

04:39.240 --> 04:42.430
Yeah? Does it involve cooking?

04:42.430 --> 04:43.590
Yeah, sort of.

04:44.030 --> 04:47.520
Then instead of just working part-time 
at a piddly café like this,

04:47.520 --> 04:52.710
shouldn't you be working a job where 
you can learn more cooking skills?

04:52.710 --> 04:55.430
That's not true at all! I mean...

04:56.840 --> 04:58.400
You mean what?

04:58.400 --> 04:59.860
Nothing.

05:00.720 --> 05:01.770
Captain!

05:03.200 --> 05:08.370
I'm permitted to unconditionally beat up 
any dude-types who come here, correct?

05:08.370 --> 05:10.870
I never authorized that action.

05:10.870 --> 05:15.370
But we're under attack by enemy units again!

05:15.370 --> 05:16.170
Enemy units?

05:16.170 --> 05:17.370
Over there!

05:17.370 --> 05:19.250
Hey! Stop it!

05:19.250 --> 05:20.990
C'mon, just sit down.

05:20.990 --> 05:22.250
Chat with us.

05:22.250 --> 05:23.770
I said, stop!

05:22.980 --> 05:24.210
Those guys...

05:25.090 --> 05:27.510
The ones who messed with us 
at the Cherry Blossom Festival...

05:28.700 --> 05:30.570
They're still pulling crap like this?

05:31.360 --> 05:32.670
Private Tsuruga!

05:32.670 --> 05:36.040
I'm giving you a mission 
to rescue Tsukishima Riho!

05:36.040 --> 05:38.340
Go ahead and scare the life out of them!

05:38.340 --> 05:39.360
Yes, sir!

05:40.710 --> 05:42.940
You boys sure are full of pep.

05:43.290 --> 05:45.720
But this is a café.

05:45.720 --> 05:48.200
How about I take your order first?

05:48.630 --> 05:50.570
Wh-Who the hell is this?

05:50.570 --> 05:52.680
Wait... That ponytail...

05:52.680 --> 05:53.700
Rustle, rustle!

05:54.190 --> 06:00.460
We have a Shoryuken, a Tatsumaki Senpukyaku, 
and our summer special, the Somersault Kick.

06:01.120 --> 06:02.460
What'll it be?

06:02.460 --> 06:03.680
She changed her mask...

06:03.680 --> 06:05.260
Wait, isn't this...

06:06.300 --> 06:10.360
Act now, and you can punch 
one of our wait staff, on the house!

06:11.180 --> 06:14.220
Immediate initiation of 
legitimate self-defense!

06:15.620 --> 06:17.180
It <i>is</i> you!

06:17.180 --> 06:18.270
Rustle, rustle, rustle!

06:19.200 --> 06:20.310
Well...

06:20.770 --> 06:23.340
Hurry up and place your order!

06:23.340 --> 06:26.030
We're busy here!

06:27.780 --> 06:31.380
That wasn't really 
what I meant by scaring them...

06:32.870 --> 06:35.100
Whoa! Akane-chan!

06:35.100 --> 06:37.020
It's kinda overflowing!

06:37.020 --> 06:39.000
You poured too much in at once.

06:39.280 --> 06:41.040
Yeah, but...

06:41.040 --> 06:42.630
I won't need you here.

06:43.240 --> 06:45.280
Go help at the beach hut.

06:45.280 --> 06:47.880
Hey! Don't give up on me!

06:48.500 --> 06:52.080
Thank you for stopping by!

06:52.080 --> 06:54.090
Thanks for the grub!

06:54.090 --> 06:57.140
Come back when Mad Dog Ouka-san is here!

06:55.350 --> 06:57.140
<b>Mad Dog</b>

06:57.140 --> 06:59.390
Like hell we will!

06:59.390 --> 07:03.270
Th-Thanks. I'm not sure what just 
happened, but you saved me there.

07:03.270 --> 07:04.020
Not at all!

07:04.020 --> 07:07.420
Hayacchi told me to come and save you!

07:07.420 --> 07:08.650
He did?

07:09.200 --> 07:12.530
Come to think of it, 
Hayacchi seemed kinda down earlier.

07:13.070 --> 07:16.410
He said he showed concern for you, 
and then you insulted him.

07:17.430 --> 07:19.800
Was he that upset?

07:19.800 --> 07:21.670
Yeah. He was making a face like this.

07:22.120 --> 07:24.950
That dork. I was just kidding around.

07:26.230 --> 07:28.760
It's not a bad feeling, though.

07:29.710 --> 07:33.050
Oh, all right. I guess I'll go apologize.

07:35.510 --> 07:37.400
See? Isn't he hot?

07:37.400 --> 07:38.520
He is!

07:38.520 --> 07:40.310
Hot <i>and</i> a Tokyo U student!

07:40.310 --> 07:41.850
Talk about high-spec!

07:41.850 --> 07:44.980
And that bit of curl to his hair is so cute!

07:44.980 --> 07:46.430
Uh...

07:47.300 --> 07:48.440
Riho?

07:49.570 --> 07:51.570
It's just naturally wavy!

07:51.570 --> 07:55.280
<b>Mad Dog Ouka-chan!</b>

07:52.260 --> 07:54.120
<i>Mad Dog Ouka-chan!</i>

07:57.450 --> 07:59.190
Th-Th-The Mad Dog!

07:59.190 --> 08:00.830
Wh-What's your problem?

08:01.840 --> 08:03.830
What's wrong with Hayato-kun?

08:04.470 --> 08:08.300
He said no breaks other than 
the Obon Festival, right?

08:08.820 --> 08:12.760
Despite how he sounded, 
I think he's just looking out for us.

08:13.130 --> 08:16.140
Yeah! We've been really busy for a long time.

08:16.140 --> 08:20.900
Plus, he was worried because 
Riho-san keeps working too hard.

08:20.900 --> 08:22.660
Wait, really?

08:23.280 --> 08:24.390
In that case...

08:24.870 --> 08:27.270
We'd better have a damn good time!

08:28.640 --> 08:30.680
The beach!

08:31.640 --> 08:34.170
Sweet! There's nobody around!

08:34.170 --> 08:35.030
You're right!

08:35.410 --> 08:37.270
Yeah, 'cause it rained all morning.

08:38.080 --> 08:40.490
It's like our own private beach!

08:45.270 --> 08:46.960
Hey, Shiragiku.

08:48.080 --> 08:50.050
Do you know where Hayato is?

08:50.050 --> 08:52.710
Hayato-kun's where he always is.

08:58.720 --> 09:00.020
Catch anything?

09:01.120 --> 09:01.970
Not really.

09:01.970 --> 09:04.650
I'm not trying to catch anything, anyway.

09:05.180 --> 09:08.270
Only people who catch 
something get to say that.

09:08.270 --> 09:09.310
Shut up.

09:10.290 --> 09:13.740
It's been years since I played 
around at the beach.

09:13.740 --> 09:17.660
I know. I think it's been 
since grade school for me.

09:17.660 --> 09:19.370
Wow, that long?

09:19.370 --> 09:22.940
Da-dun... Da-dun...

09:20.850 --> 09:24.110
Now that you mention it, whenever we 
went to a pool or beach in grade school,

09:24.110 --> 09:26.400
there was always some boy 
who peed in the water.

09:26.400 --> 09:28.540
Farting's one thing, but...

09:31.670 --> 09:33.880
Did... you just fart?

09:33.880 --> 09:35.690
Um... Are you okay?

09:35.690 --> 09:37.680
N-No way! I did not!

09:37.680 --> 09:41.310
That wasn't me! I didn't fart!

09:42.680 --> 09:46.310
I was thinking about a new song. A summery one.

09:46.670 --> 09:50.060
Yeah? As a fan, 
I'm looking forward to hearing it.

09:50.060 --> 09:52.520
Make it as exciting as your usual stuff.

09:52.940 --> 09:55.720
Nope, this one's a ballad.

09:57.460 --> 09:59.940
My first... love song.

10:00.830 --> 10:04.240
Hey! I bet it was Ami-chan playing a prank!

10:04.240 --> 10:07.930
I know you're there! Get out here, Ami-chan!

10:10.020 --> 10:10.840
So...

10:11.250 --> 10:13.430
Want to hear the lyrics?

10:18.370 --> 10:20.840
What the heck is this?! It's crazy strong!

10:21.400 --> 10:22.540
Hey! The lyrics!

10:22.540 --> 10:25.220
Later! I've got a big one on—

10:28.290 --> 10:29.980
Ta-da! It was m—

10:39.700 --> 10:41.610
That was so much fun!

10:41.610 --> 10:43.740
Ami-chan, you seem kinda down.

10:43.740 --> 10:46.040
Hayacchi chewed me out bigtime.

10:46.040 --> 10:47.500
Damn right I did.

10:47.880 --> 10:50.890
Anyway, Ouka, I heard you farted in the water?

10:50.890 --> 10:52.360
I did not!

10:52.360 --> 10:54.040
Ami told me you did.

10:54.350 --> 10:55.260
Ami-chan!

10:55.260 --> 10:56.550
She bolted!

10:58.470 --> 11:00.110
Come on in!

11:00.110 --> 11:03.800
If you need a break, 
try out Seaside Café Familia!

11:03.800 --> 11:05.480
Hey, isn't this the place?

11:06.260 --> 11:09.080
The one with the cute girls 
that's all the rage on the internet?

11:09.080 --> 11:11.020
Yep! This is the place!

11:11.020 --> 11:12.520
Order up.

11:13.540 --> 11:16.060
Got another order. Three watermelon parfaits.

11:16.060 --> 11:17.130
Got it.

11:17.130 --> 11:19.230
What a crowd, huh?

11:19.230 --> 11:22.570
Yeah. Must be thanks to 
our chief of promotions, Riho.

11:22.570 --> 11:23.530
Must be.

11:23.880 --> 11:25.740
She really is a customer service genius.

11:26.090 --> 11:28.160
I'm so glad we have her.

11:28.160 --> 11:30.000
Have a seat right over here.

11:30.270 --> 11:34.040
Oh, our summer-only 
watermelon parfait is really good!

11:34.040 --> 11:35.320
Hey, lady!

11:35.320 --> 11:36.380
Coming!

11:36.380 --> 11:39.470
I told her to take a break.

11:40.770 --> 11:42.880
Sure is slow here.

11:43.230 --> 11:47.240
Hayato will yell at you again 
for serving customers in that thing.

11:48.920 --> 11:52.350
No problem! I'll take it off if any come in!

11:54.500 --> 11:55.690
Hey, Ami...

11:56.010 --> 11:59.500
If you're that bored, 
want to practice making coffee?

11:59.500 --> 12:01.320
Yeah! Let's do it!

12:01.950 --> 12:03.270
A break?

12:03.840 --> 12:05.200
I don't need one yet.

12:05.200 --> 12:08.090
I'm having everyone do equal work.

12:08.090 --> 12:09.200
Besides,

12:09.550 --> 12:12.960
you didn't even eat breakfast because 
you said you had prep work to do.

12:12.960 --> 12:15.330
Yeah, but we're getting 
a ton of customers right now.

12:15.330 --> 12:16.780
No! Take a break!

12:16.780 --> 12:19.640
If you won't do as your 
boss says, you'll be fired.

12:24.380 --> 12:27.880
Yep! The staff meals you make 
are always the best, Kiku-chan!

12:27.880 --> 12:29.720
You can eat a little slower.

12:29.720 --> 12:31.460
Fine!

12:31.460 --> 12:34.850
And I think you could probably 
slow down your work pace, too.

12:34.850 --> 12:37.860
I know what Hayato-kun said to you,

12:38.370 --> 12:40.780
but I think he's just really worried.

12:41.500 --> 12:42.760
Excuse me.

12:42.760 --> 12:43.850
Coming.

12:45.570 --> 12:46.990
I know that.

12:47.610 --> 12:50.960
It's just that I'm really happy.

12:50.960 --> 12:51.660
Huh?

12:52.500 --> 12:55.910
It feels good being needed 
so much by someone.

12:57.680 --> 12:58.630
How's this?

12:58.630 --> 13:00.030
Well, Akane-san?

13:00.030 --> 13:02.630
Oh... Yeah. Not bad, actually.

13:02.630 --> 13:04.830
Well, it's just pouring water in, right?

13:04.830 --> 13:07.440
Anyone can do that!

13:07.440 --> 13:08.640
You'd think so.

13:08.970 --> 13:11.890
Okay, I'll teach you in 
a little more detail now.

13:12.360 --> 13:14.110
Yes, Coffee Master!

13:14.110 --> 13:16.270
Don't call me that.

13:17.270 --> 13:19.240
Got a summer cold? Figures.

13:19.240 --> 13:20.010
Snap!

13:20.010 --> 13:22.380
What's that mean?! You saying I'm stupid?!

13:22.380 --> 13:24.280
Um, excuse me.

13:24.840 --> 13:26.570
I'm with TTS TV,

13:26.570 --> 13:30.780
and I'd like to interview you 
for a news feature on beach huts.

13:30.780 --> 13:31.560
Huh?

13:31.560 --> 13:35.400
We heard one of your waitresses here 
was getting rave reviews.

13:35.400 --> 13:38.790
Wow! They must be talking about Riho-san!

13:38.790 --> 13:41.210
Sure, that's fine. Riho is—

13:41.210 --> 13:43.170
My break's over now!

13:44.370 --> 13:46.630
Wait, what's all the fuss in here?

13:46.630 --> 13:47.760
Wait...

13:48.140 --> 13:50.890
Riho-chan? As in Tsukishima Riho?

13:51.230 --> 13:53.100
Huh? Uh, yes...

13:53.100 --> 13:54.200
I knew it!

13:54.200 --> 13:56.980
I used to work on a variety show 
with you! Remember me?

13:57.260 --> 14:00.980
I guess not, huh? 
I was still just an AD then.

14:00.980 --> 14:02.650
Uh... Hi.

14:03.120 --> 14:05.990
It's good to see you again, Nomura-san.

14:05.990 --> 14:08.400
Oh, you <i>do</i> remember me!

14:08.400 --> 14:09.530
You know each other?

14:09.530 --> 14:11.520
Idiot! How can you not know her?

14:11.520 --> 14:14.430
This is the genius child star who got her 
big break fifteen years ago,

14:14.430 --> 14:16.250
Tsukishima Riho!

14:16.950 --> 14:20.810
Um, I'm sorry, but I'd rather 
not talk about my past.

14:20.810 --> 14:22.000
Oh, sorry.

14:22.340 --> 14:24.750
A child star? Riho-san?

14:25.200 --> 14:27.310
They just said that's Tsukishima Riho!

14:27.310 --> 14:28.760
Huh? Who?

14:28.760 --> 14:31.760
Come to think of it, 
she used to be on TV all the time!

14:32.310 --> 14:34.400
But then she just sorta disappeared.

14:34.400 --> 14:36.590
She had black hair and a nice, clean look.

14:36.590 --> 14:38.540
She's sure lost her innocence.

14:38.540 --> 14:41.900
She was such a star, and now that 
she's grown, she's working part-time?

14:41.900 --> 14:43.770
What a fall from grace.

14:48.180 --> 14:51.020
Um... Riho-chan...

14:54.470 --> 14:55.660
Riho-san!

14:56.080 --> 14:59.020
Aw, damn. I shouldn't have done that.

14:59.440 --> 15:00.330
Shiragiku,

15:00.330 --> 15:02.090
go check on her.

15:02.090 --> 15:03.390
S-Sure!

15:03.840 --> 15:05.930
Ouka, go get Ami.

15:05.930 --> 15:07.590
Two of you won't be enough 
to handle all this.

15:07.590 --> 15:09.520
Uh... Sure.

15:13.220 --> 15:14.300
Hey...

15:14.300 --> 15:16.720
Why isn't Riho-san here?

15:16.720 --> 15:17.950
Why?!

15:17.950 --> 15:20.230
She said she's not feeling well.

15:20.230 --> 15:23.420
But we promised we'd all eat meals together!

15:23.420 --> 15:24.920
Shut up and eat.

15:25.480 --> 15:27.120
You can have my Hamburg steak.

15:27.120 --> 15:28.110
Really?!

15:28.110 --> 15:31.110
Yay! Hamburg!

15:32.530 --> 15:34.120
I'm sorry, Riho.

15:34.520 --> 15:37.870
I can't be with you anymore.

15:38.300 --> 15:43.180
But why?! I've been working 
so hard for you and Mom!

15:43.970 --> 15:46.490
<i>Then I'll work even harder!</i>

15:46.490 --> 15:48.630
<i>Please don't go away!</i>

15:56.600 --> 15:58.800
<i>Help, Ululman!</i>

15:58.800 --> 16:01.100
<i>The monster's gonna eat everyone!</i>

16:01.100 --> 16:04.600
<i>Please save us, Ululman!</i>

16:05.810 --> 16:08.360
<i>Was she that big a deal as a child actress?</i>

16:09.090 --> 16:11.120
Yeah, she was huge.

16:11.120 --> 16:13.610
You could probably find videos 
if you searched for them.

16:14.000 --> 16:18.270
But her mother... well, 
she was very passionate.

16:18.270 --> 16:22.200
Some said she was overworking her daughter.

16:23.100 --> 16:26.380
Her husband wasn't too happy about that,

16:26.760 --> 16:30.490
so he asked the TV station 
not to push her too hard.

16:31.830 --> 16:33.340
Riho-san...

16:34.640 --> 16:35.840
<i>Aw, man.</i>

16:36.400 --> 16:38.940
I guess everyone knows now.

16:38.940 --> 16:43.270
I was hoping no one stopping by a run-down 
old café by the beach would recognize me...

16:44.190 --> 16:47.730
But I guess I brought it 
upon myself in the end.

16:49.570 --> 16:51.190
Pretty stupid, huh?

16:52.070 --> 16:53.350
Riho-chan...

16:53.900 --> 16:56.910
<i>Thank you, Ululman!</i>

16:58.220 --> 17:02.540
<i>Then, around when she started 
showing up on TV less often...</i>

17:04.280 --> 17:10.200
<i>I started hearing rumors that 
Riho-chan's parents had divorced.</i>

17:13.040 --> 17:16.180
Riho, please don't work too hard.

17:16.880 --> 17:18.800
I'm worried about your health.

17:19.910 --> 17:21.960
Don't worry! I'm okay!

17:21.960 --> 17:24.810
And I'll work even harder! Watch me, Dad!

17:26.260 --> 17:31.320
I mean, my mom gave me so much 
praise when I worked hard.

17:32.240 --> 17:34.170
Besides, it didn't make sense.

17:34.650 --> 17:36.950
If he was that worried about me,

17:36.950 --> 17:38.220
then why...

17:38.820 --> 17:40.830
So this is where you were.

17:42.500 --> 17:44.160
I've been looking for you.

17:45.350 --> 17:48.190
Hayato-kun... Why?

17:48.190 --> 17:51.210
Shiragiku said your dinner's in the fridge,

17:51.210 --> 17:53.370
so eat it if you're hungry.

17:54.580 --> 17:57.370
You came out here just to tell me that?

17:57.370 --> 17:58.680
Yeah, and also...

17:59.040 --> 18:01.950
It seems like I had the wrong idea.

18:01.950 --> 18:02.700
Huh?

18:03.140 --> 18:07.760
I thought your sociable nature 
was a talent you were born with,

18:07.760 --> 18:08.740
but it's not.

18:09.580 --> 18:11.060
When I thought about it, I realized

18:11.450 --> 18:16.250
it's a trade skill you obtained 
through hard work just to get by in life.

18:21.520 --> 18:23.790
That was what I had in mind, at least.

18:24.680 --> 18:27.260
The world and the TV industry are both harsh.

18:27.260 --> 18:30.780
Once I grew up, they all 
latched onto a new child star

18:30.780 --> 18:32.730
and wouldn't even look at me anymore.

18:33.920 --> 18:36.650
In the end, child stars are disposable.

18:36.650 --> 18:40.490
Some other kid who looked like me would 
just be forced to do the same stuff I did.

18:41.050 --> 18:46.060
No amount of polite behavior or sucking up 
to important people did any good.

18:46.720 --> 18:48.660
None of it meant a thing.

18:49.130 --> 18:51.800
All it did was tear my family apart.

18:52.640 --> 18:54.070
What a laugh.

18:55.170 --> 18:57.680
Regardless of your family situation,

18:57.680 --> 19:03.370
your sociable nature is indispensable 
to this café, both now and in the future.

19:03.370 --> 19:04.060
Huh?

19:04.450 --> 19:07.660
The reason business has been 
so much better than I expected,

19:07.660 --> 19:10.280
and the reason we were able 
to open the beach hut,

19:10.280 --> 19:12.170
was because we had you.

19:12.880 --> 19:17.960
So, ultimately, the work you put in when 
you were a child star did have meaning.

19:18.300 --> 19:21.720
And right now, above all, 
I'm really grateful to you.

19:22.800 --> 19:26.720
Thanks for looking after Grandma's café.

19:32.550 --> 19:33.950
I...

19:33.950 --> 19:37.730
But you said we were your family, didn't you?

19:37.730 --> 19:41.990
If we are, then no matter how 
the rest of them feel about it,

19:41.990 --> 19:47.750
I, at the very least, don't want to put more 
stress on one family member than the others.

19:48.610 --> 19:49.750
And yet...

19:51.000 --> 19:53.080
What's your deal?

19:53.360 --> 19:56.870
I keep telling you not to overdo it, 
because I'm worried about you!

19:59.160 --> 20:00.720
B-But...

20:00.720 --> 20:02.030
No buts!

20:02.030 --> 20:04.930
I'm sick of saying it over and over! 
This is the last time!

20:09.520 --> 20:10.540
But...

20:10.540 --> 20:13.710
<i>Riho, please don't work too hard.</i>

20:13.710 --> 20:16.040
<i>I'm worried about your health.</i>

20:18.480 --> 20:22.150
Then don't go away!

20:22.400 --> 20:25.530
What? I'm not going anywhere! 
Stop crying, you idiot!

20:25.930 --> 20:27.750
I'm so glad!

20:28.740 --> 20:29.540
Hey!

20:29.540 --> 20:31.080
What are you doing?!

20:31.080 --> 20:34.120
I'll stay here with you, Hayato-kun!

20:34.120 --> 20:36.860
I'll always be here!

20:38.520 --> 20:40.760
Okay, okay! Just get off me!

20:40.760 --> 20:42.960
Pat my head, then!

20:42.960 --> 20:44.300
Don't be a baby!

20:47.800 --> 20:49.930
What? You knew?

20:49.930 --> 20:52.720
Yeah. I saw you on TV all the time.

20:52.720 --> 20:56.060
I thought that must be who you were 
when I heard your name, too.

20:56.060 --> 20:58.860
But whoever you are, you're still Riho.

20:58.860 --> 21:02.110
What you were in the past doesn't matter.

21:02.110 --> 21:04.140
Now, you're just part of the family.

21:04.140 --> 21:04.780
Yep!

21:04.780 --> 21:06.110
That's right!

21:07.380 --> 21:08.630
You guys...

21:09.620 --> 21:12.920
I saw the videos! You were such a cutie!

21:12.920 --> 21:13.530
Hey!

21:13.530 --> 21:16.110
You grew up so big! 
Your big sister is so happy!

21:16.110 --> 21:19.360
Did you actually meet Ululman?! 
Was he really that strong?!

21:19.360 --> 21:22.130
Come on! You're burning my head!

21:22.720 --> 21:25.660
Just cut it out already! 
I'm the big sister here!

21:25.660 --> 21:27.970
And Ululman is just a costume!

21:29.600 --> 21:32.400
Oh, good! You're back to the usual Riho-san!

21:32.400 --> 21:33.750
Just a costume?

21:34.180 --> 21:37.370
Enough being dumb! It's time to get to work!

21:38.590 --> 21:39.400
Hey.

21:40.500 --> 21:41.320
Listen...

21:41.710 --> 21:44.840
That crying yesterday... 
It was all just an act.

21:44.840 --> 21:46.570
Don't take it seriously, okay?

21:47.810 --> 21:49.030
Oh, really?

21:49.420 --> 21:51.280
Well, that's a genius child star for you.

21:51.280 --> 21:52.960
That's "<i>super</i> genius child star"!

21:52.960 --> 21:55.360
Wah! Don't go away!

21:55.360 --> 21:56.380
Hey!

23:27.050 --> 23:41.980
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

23:27.050 --> 23:41.980
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

23:27.530 --> 23:30.730
So you had the clean, 
black-haired look back then, huh?

23:30.730 --> 23:32.750
But that would overlap with Shiragiku-san—

23:33.140 --> 23:36.700
Hayato-kun! Let's lock ourselves 
in a hot, sweaty grapple!

23:36.700 --> 23:38.980
Stop it!

23:38.980 --> 23:41.630
Oh, yeah, I guess <i>that</i> 
doesn't overlap with anyone.
